                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Balliol College (Domus de Balliolo)</orgName><p>Notes of pledging‘On 2 at
                        the top is an erased inscription, perhaps of an early owner [...] The late
                        14th-cent. College inventory-mark 249 liber theologie is at the head of 7,
                        and the valuation precium xvi s. on 8. On 6v is a 15th-cent. title. At the
                        foot of 1 (the old pastedown) is a horizontal staple-mark.’ (Mynors,
                        Balliol, 319)‘Liber Willelmi de Wilton . . . super iiij libros Sent. Item
                        idem super sacramenta altaris’ (fol. 2)‘Iste liber est collegii de Ballolo
                        in Oxon’ ex legato magistri Willemi Wylton’ quondam cancellarii
                        universitatis Oxon’ ac socii eiusdem domus cuius anime | propicietur Deus et
                        est inceptor Ockham super quattuor libros Sententiarum et super sacramenta
                        altaris’ (fol. 2)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">William Wilton (d. after 1376), fellow of
                     Balliol, chancellor of Oxford</provenance>
